<h1><span lang="EN-US">Capture 2D Point</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Capture 2D Point</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">allows a datum point to be captured using the localiser probe and then to compensate with the probe diameter. It is used to</font></span> <span lang="EN-US">get the co-ordinates of feature points on flat areas of an object. Another application of this command is to build datum alignments from point, line, and plane, from known points, or from three points. This command is accessible from the</span> <span lang="EN-US" class="Path" style="font-style:normal;">Localiser</span> <span class="Path" style="font-style:normal;">Menu</span> <span class="Path">Datum &gt; 2D Point</span><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-US">Wizard</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-US">When you select</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Datum &gt; 2D Point</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">from the localiser menu, the following dialogue will appear:</span></p>
<p><img src="../Capture_files/capture_2D_point.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">At this stage there are offered 2 possibilities for measuring the 2D point:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">If you press<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'B'</b></span> button, you will capture a<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Surface Point</b></span> - In this case only one set of points is captured and used for both plane and point definition. See <a href="#Capture_Surface_Point_Wizard">Surface Point Wizard</a>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">If you press <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'A'</b></span> button, you will capture a<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Planar Point</b></span> - the procedure goes in 2 steps:</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul type="circle" class="whs5">
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal-bullet">
<p class="Normal-bullet">capture of set of points for plane definition (the plane, where the point lies).</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNormal-bullet">
<p class="Normal-bullet">capture of set of points to define the point itself.<br>
See <a href="#Capture_Planar_Point_Wizard">Planar Point Wizard</a>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>&#160;</p>
<h3><span lang="EN-US"><a name="Capture_Surface_Point_Wizard"></a>Capture Surface Point Wizard</span></h3>
<p><span lang="EN-US">You have chosen the Surface Point Capture and you should capture now the whole set of points.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP936219103" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Capture_files/surface_point.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Press '</font></span><span class="Button">B'</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">button at least three times to collect the necessary points.</font></span> <span lang="EN-GB">Hold</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'B'</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">button to delete the last captured point if necessary.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Press '</font></span><span class="Button">A'</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">button to finish. The plane where the point lies, is defined.</font></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Direction of the plane normal is automatically calculated based on the orientation of the last axis.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">If you use ball probe this will offset the plane with the radius of the probe at the proper direction. This is very important for the correct location of the plane because every arm returns co-ordinates of the centre of its probe.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Scheme</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP935580888" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Capture_files/image14.gif" width="443px" height="239px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">KUBE will fit a point from the set of the captured points and will offset it along the plane normal with the probe radius. The following information about the resulting point will be displayed:</font></span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Co-ordinates of the point.</font></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Maximal distance between the captured points.</font></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">RMS of the point fit.</font></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-US">Plane fit RMS. It will be zero if you captured three points.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a4" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP224110125" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Capture_files/surface_point_3.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<ul class="whs7">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Press '</font></span><span class="Button">A'</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">button to reject the resulting point or '</font></span><span class="Button">B'</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">button to create it.</font></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">After finishing the capture procedure, KUBE will issue a dialog, asking you if you will continue capturing surface/planar points.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a5" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP1044233633" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Capture_files/continue.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Press '</span><span class="Button">A'</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button to exit the capture mode or '</span><span class="Button">B'</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button to continue capturing.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>&#160;</p>
<h3><span lang="EN-US"><a name="Capture_Planar_Point_Wizard"></a>Capture Planar Point Wizard</span></h3>
<p><span lang="EN-US">You have chosen the Planar Point Capture and you should capture first the set of points for plane definition.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a6" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP224315752" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Capture_files/capture_define_plane.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Press '</font></span><span class="Button">B'</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">button at least three times to collect the necessary points.</font></span> <span lang="EN-GB">Hold</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'B'</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">button to delete the last captured point if necessary.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Press '</font></span><span class="Button">A'</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">button to finish. The plane where the point lies, is defined.</font></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Direction of the plane normal is automatically calculated based on the orientation of the last axis.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span lang="EN-US">If you use ball probe this will offset the plane with the radius of the probe at the proper direction. This is very important for the correct location of the plane because every arm returns co-ordinates of the centre of its probe.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a8" style="text-decoration:underline;">Scheme</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP235978129" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Capture_files/image14.gif" width="443px" height="239px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</div>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Now you have to capture the point/set of points to be compensated.</font></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a11" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP225621364" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Capture_files/surface_point_4.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<ul>
<li style="font-size:10.0pt;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Press '</span><span class="Button">B'</span> <span lang="EN-US">button once or more times to get the point. Press '</span><span class="Button">A'</span> <span lang="EN-US">button to finish.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-US">KUBE will fit a point from the set of the captured points and will offset it along the normal of the captured plane with the probe radius. The following information about the resulting point will be displayed:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-US">co-ordinates of the point.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-US">maximal distance between the captured points.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-US">RMS of the point fit (it will be zero if one point only is captured).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Plane fit RMS (it will be zero if you captured three points).</font></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a9" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP226827297" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Capture_files/surface_point_5.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<ul class="whs7">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Press '</font></span><span class="Button">A'</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">button to reject the resulting point or '</font></span><span class="Button">B'</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">button to create it.</font></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: If Stream of points method is used then a compensated datum point is created each time the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'B'</b></span> button is pressed and no Accept/Reject dialog appears. See <span lang="EN-GB"><a href="../../References/Preferences_-_Datums_-_Capture_Method.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Datums &gt; Capture Method (Point Capture Method)</a> for details.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">After finishing the capture procedure, KUBE will issue a dialog, asking you if you will continue capturing 2D points.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a10" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP288796681" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../Capture_files/continue.gif" width="766px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
</div>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Press '</span><span class="Button">A'</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button to exit the capture mode or '</span><span class="Button">B'</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button to continue capturing.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
